     1  *        *>--- conformance-case
     2  *        *> id: pb5987-declaratives-after-section
     3  *        *> rules: [FMT-14.2.1]
     4  *        *> source-format: free
     5  *        *> portable: unverified
     6  *        *>---
     7  *              *> kb/Work PB5987. §1985:IV.6.4.1.1: "Declarative sections must be grouped
        +         at the beginning of the Procedure
     8  *              *> Division" (§2023:14.3 the same): a DECLARATIVES portion written after a
        +         nondeclarative section is refused by
     9  *              *> that ordering rule (COBOL2797), never as a reserved word used as a user
        +        -defined word.
    10                  IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
    11                  PROGRAM-ID. PB5987AS.
    12                  ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
    13                  INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
    14                  FILE-CONTROL.
    15                      SELECT F ASSIGN TO "PB5987AS.TMP".
    16                  DATA DIVISION.
    17                  FILE SECTION.
    18                  FD F.
    19                  01 F-REC PIC X(4).
    20                  PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    21                  MAIN-S SECTION.
    22                  MAIN-P.
    23                      DISPLAY "B".
    24                      STOP RUN.
    25                  DECLARATIVES.
                        ^
                 ==> error COBOL2797 (col 8): PROCEDURE DIVISION: a DECLARATIVES portion that follows a nondeclarative section,
                     paragraph or sentence — §1985:IV.6.4.1.1: "Declarative sections must be grouped at the beginning of the
                     Procedure Division", so §1985:IV.6.4.1.4.2 Format 1 prints the DECLARATIVES … END DECLARATIVES portion
                     immediately after the procedure division header.
    26                  ERR-S SECTION.
    27                      USE AFTER STANDARD ERROR PROCEDURE ON F.
    28                  ERR-P.
    29                      DISPLAY "IN-DECLARATIVES".
    30                  END DECLARATIVES.
    31
